  "source": "https://gc.nh.gov/rsa/html/LXIII/660/660-18.htm",
  "statuteText": "660:18 Notice. –\n\nWhenever any person intends to contest the election of a state senator or representative, he shall send to him a notice in writing of such contest with the reasons therefor, citing the acts constituting the violation and, if known, the specific sections of the law or of the constitution being violated. The notice shall be sent by certified mail and postmarked on or before the December 15 immediately following the election. At the same time the notice is sent to the senator or representative, a copy thereof shall be sent to the secretary of state."
}
